# Reference copy of the site block appended to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile on wharf (VM 102).
# `acme_dns_opts` is the existing snippet in that file (Linode DNS-01, token from
# /etc/caddy/environment). Apply manually; wharf's sudo requires a password:
#   ssh -t jcz@192.0.2.254 'sudo caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile \
#     --adapter caddyfile --envfile /etc/caddy/environment && sudo systemctl reload caddy'
# Pre-change backup on wharf: ~/Caddyfile.pre-pelias-orig

# Pelias Maine geocoder - VM 120 pelias-maine (192.0.2.20), nginx edge on 8080
#
# The edge refuses /v1/* without a known API key (docs/API_KEYS.md). Caddy presents the "demo" key
# on behalf of every public visitor, so the demo page needs no key of its own and no key is visible
# to the browser. The consequence is deliberate: at this hostname the key is labelling and rate
# limiting, not access control - whoever can reach the URL is "demo". Traffic sent straight to
# 192.0.2.20:8080 still has to carry its own key. To revoke: drop the demo entry from
# edge_api_keys in zz-local.yml, re-run the edge role, and put the replacement key here.
# The real key is not in this file; it lives in the password manager and in /etc/caddy/Caddyfile.
geocoder.example.org {
	import acme_dns_opts
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 192.0.2.20:8080 {
		header_up X-API-Key "pgeo_REPLACE_WITH_THE_DEMO_KEY"
	}
}
